      "summary": {
        "unit_id": "hmh07-lua-follow3:145",
        "answer": "Registers keyboard left/right and optional confirm callbacks. Each first honors the supplied controller predicate and menu navigation-disable state. Successful left/right navigation selects the active widget and processes its list action; the handlers still return true after an allowed route even if navigation fails. The confirm callback is omitted when PC selection behavior is already enabled; its allowed path selects the element, processes its action and plays the configured/default sound. Actual event delivery and list method implementations remain external. For CoD.GridAndListUtility.MakeBumperGridKeyboardNavigable, evaluate the displayed formal inputs and captured values. Its exact paths are 71: if f5_arg4 and not f5_arg4( controller ) then; 72: return; 73: elseif menu.m_disableGridNavigation then; 74: return; 75: elseif not f5_arg1.m_disableNavigation and f5_arg1:navigateItemLeft(  [excerpt; exact source record identified separately]",
